            "review_title": "Review at Bun Cha Number 1",
            "review_text": "Nam Nguyen\n2 contributions\n0\nDecent restaurant for experiencing the atmosphere in the middle of Hanoi\nOct 2021 • Friends\nSince I'm a local, this place was pretty expensive for us and the price was a bit higher than most of the same street restaurants here in the Old Quarter. We simply ordered two serves and the portion was modest, each cost around $2 ( the average price for a same one this type was $1.5 ). The restaurant itself was kinda small with plastic chairs and tables like many other street restaurants ( kinda clean though ) , the atmosphere was decent, staff is helpful,fast but we ordered for half a plate of broth he gave us a full plate which ended up wasted. The meal was decent ( but the meat was good ). If you want to have a dish here the street where you can hear motorbikes zoom by, I highly recommended this place.\nRead more\nWritten October 17, 2021",
            "rating": 5.0,
